# 🚀 Storyteller Suite — Full Deployment Guide

From GitHub Codespaces → Docker Image → DockerHub → Production Stack

---

## Part 1 — Setting Up in GitHub Codespaces

### Step 1: Open the Branch in Codespaces

1. Go to **https://github.com/iamadoctorforreal/Video-Generator-Workflow**
2. Click the **Branch** dropdown and select **`storyteller-suite-latest-update-28-06-2026`**
3. Click the green **`<> Code`** button → click the **`Codespaces`** tab → click **`Create codespace on this branch`**
4. Wait ~2 minutes for the environment to boot up. You will get a full VS Code editor in your browser.

---

### Step 2: Install Dependencies

In the Codespaces terminal, run:

```bash
pip install -r requirements-cpu.txt
```

> [!NOTE]
> This uses the CPU build of PyTorch. It will take 3–5 minutes in Codespaces. The app will run, just slower than on a GPU machine.

---

### Step 3: Fix ImageMagick Security Policy (Required for Captions)

```bash
sudo sed -i 's/rights="none" pattern="@\*"/rights="read|write" pattern="@\*"/g' /etc/ImageMagick-6/policy.xml
```

---

### Step 4: Test the App Runs

```bash
python app.py
```

Codespaces will automatically detect port `8000` and offer to open it. Click **Open in Browser** to confirm the Studio UI loads correctly.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Press `Ctrl+C` to stop the app before building the Docker image. You don't need to keep it running.

---

## Part 2 — Building the Docker Image

Your project already has a [Dockerfile](file:///c:/Users/RUKAYYAH%20IBRAHIM/Desktop/video-generator-workflow/Dockerfile) that handles everything (ffmpeg, imagemagick, Python dependencies, etc.).

### Step 5: Log In to DockerHub

```bash
docker login
```

Enter your DockerHub **username** and **password** when prompted.

---

### Step 6: Build the Image

Replace `yourdockerhubusername` with your actual DockerHub username:

```bash
docker build -t okayna/storyteller-suite:latest .
```

> [!NOTE]
> This step downloads ~2GB of dependencies and will take **10–20 minutes** in Codespaces on the free tier. This is a one-time cost — future rebuilds are much faster due to Docker layer caching.

---

### Step 7: Push to DockerHub

```bash
docker push okayna/storyteller-suite:latest
```

Once complete, your image will be publicly available at:
`https://hub.docker.com/r/yourdockerhubusername/storyteller-suite`

---

## Part 3 — Running the Full Stack from Docker

This is the exciting part. Your [docker-compose.yml](file:///c:/Users/RUKAYYAH%20IBRAHIM/Desktop/video-generator-workflow/docker-compose.yml) already defines **both services** together:

| Service | Container Name | Port |
|---|---|---|
| FastAPI Video App | `kokoro-video-api` | `8000` |
| n8n Automation | `kokoro-n8n` | `5678` |

### Step 8: Update docker-compose.yml to Use Your DockerHub Image

On any machine where you want to run this, edit `docker-compose.yml` and change the `video-generator` service from building locally to pulling your published image:

```yaml
services:
  video-generator:
    image: yourdockerhubusername/storyteller-suite:latest  # ← Use this instead of build: .
    container_name: kokoro-video-api
    ports:
      - "8000:8000"
    volumes:
      - ./videos:/app/temp_uploads   # Persist generated videos
      - ./uploads:/app/images        # Persist uploaded images
    environment:
      - PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
    restart: unless-stopped

  n8n:
    image: n8nio/n8n:latest
    container_name: kokoro-n8n
    ports:
      - "5678:5678"
    environment:
      - N8N_PORT=5678
      - N8N_PROTOCOL=http
      - N8N_ENFORCE_SETTINGS_FILE_PERMISSIONS=false
      - N8N_DIAGNOSTICS_ENABLED=false
    volumes:
      - n8n_data:/home/node/.n8n
    restart: unless-stopped
    depends_on:
      - video-generator

volumes:
  n8n_data:
```

### Step 9: Start the Full Stack

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

- The `-d` flag runs everything in the background (detached mode).
- Both containers start automatically. `n8n` waits for `video-generator` to be ready first (due to `depends_on`).

### Step 10: Access the Apps

| App | URL |
|---|---|
| Storyteller Studio UI | http://localhost:8000 |
| n8n Automation Dashboard | http://localhost:5678 |

To stop everything:
```bash
docker compose down
```

